Let the Living Gear Shadow Dance perk (Rogue Subtlety) use
stealth-only openers (Ambush, Garrote, etc.) without actually being
stealthed.
Touches: src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp, Spell::CheckCast()

Why: the stealth-only gate is a single, precise check --
SPELL_ATTR0_ONLY_STEALTHED + !HasStealthAura() -> SPELL_FAILED_ONLY_STEALTHED.
Faking a real stealth aura instead of patching this check would also
apply stealth's visual crouch/transparency and detection-range penalty,
which isn't what "openers usable anytime, permanent buff" is supposed to
feel like. LivingGear_BypassStealthRequirement (LivingGear_Perks.cpp)
checks Subtlety spec + the Shadow Dance perk; skip this patch and
Subtlety rogues keep the normal stealth requirement on those abilities,
the rest of the perk (the party/raid attack power buff) is unaffected.

--- a/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
@@ (near the top, alongside the existing LivingGear_AccountLockpickSkill forward-declare)
 uint32 LivingGear_AccountLockpickSkill(Player* player);
+// Living Gear core-patch: Shadow Dance lets stealth-only openers be used
+// without actually being stealthed (LivingGear_Perks.cpp).
+bool LivingGear_BypassStealthRequirement(Unit* caster);

@@ Spell::CheckCast(bool strict)
-            if (m_spellInfo->HasAttribute(SPELL_ATTR0_ONLY_STEALTHED) && !(m_caster->HasStealthAura()))
+            if (m_spellInfo->HasAttribute(SPELL_ATTR0_ONLY_STEALTHED) && !(m_caster->HasStealthAura())
+                    && !LivingGear_BypassStealthRequirement(m_caster))
                 return SPELL_FAILED_ONLY_STEALTHED;
